<h3>Services for students needing accommodations</h3>

<p>It is the policy and practice of SIUE to create inclusive learning
environments. If aspects of the instruction or design of this course create
barriers to your inclusion or to accurate assessment of achievement, please
contact <a href="https://www.siue.edu/access/">Accessible Campus Community and
Equitable Student Support (ACCESS)</a> as soon as possible. Register with ACCESS
online at <a href="https://www.siue.edu/access/">siue.edu/access</a> or in person
in the Student Success Center, Room 1203. Email
<a href="mailto:myaccess@siue.edu">myaccess@siue.edu</a> or call
<a href="tel:+16186503726">618-650-3726</a>.</p>

<p>Accommodations are not a favor and they are not remedial. Tell me what you
need and we will make it work.</p>

<h3>Cougar Care</h3>

<p>College life can be challenging, and I support students prioritizing their
mental health. Counseling is available at the Student Success Center, Room 0222.
Make an appointment at
<a href="https://cougarcare.siue.edu/">cougarcare.siue.edu</a> or call
<a href="tel:+16186502842">618-650-2842</a>.</p>

